+# Mutation cycles from reddening sequences — verified generator
+
+| Profile field | Value |
+|---|---|
+| Track | **B** — an efficient exact algorithm exists and is reported |
+| Native domain | combinatorics |
+| Object regime | finite discrete |
+| Computational core | other (weighted-quiver mutation) |
+| Certificate | exact symbolic reduced mutation word |
+| Intended intuition | change of variables: conjugate an acyclic source cycle |
+| Domain essentiality | native; no reduction or surrogate |
+
+## Problem and trust model
+
+The generator turns Ervin and Neville's [*Mutation Cycles from Reddening
+Sequences*](https://arxiv.org/abs/2504.06573) into an exact witness task.  A solver
+receives a labelled 4-by-4 integer exchange matrix and must return a reduced
+vertex word of a specified length whose quiver mutations return the matrix
+exactly.  `verify` checks shape and reducedness and replays Definition 2.2 with
+integers; it never reads `inst["answer"]`.
+
+Generation is inverse/theorem-backed.  It samples an abundant acyclic
+three-vertex quiver, chooses the alternating conjugator
+`M=(middle, endpoint)^q`, mutates that block, adjoins a fourth source, and carries
+the known word `4, M^-1, S, M` through a random relabelling.  Theorem 4.21 proves
+closure, Theorem 4.23 proves simplicity, and Theorem 4.27 proves that in this
+rank-four regime it is the unique simple cycle.
+
+## Why Track B
+
+This is not a Track-A complexity claim.  Lemma 3.11 identifies the easy core:
+an abundant acyclic quiver's unique reduced reddening sequence is its source
+sequence.  Mechanically, the reference algorithm finds the unique decreasing
+mutation of the cyclic rank-three block at every step, reaches that acyclic
+core, takes its source order, and retraces the descent.  It is
+`O(L r^3)` exact arithmetic (`r=4`); at shipping size it performs **24 trial
+mutations and 329 conservatively counted scalar operations per instance** and
+solves 8/8.  The measured eight-instance run is recorded in
+`selftest_report.json`.
+
+The compact route notices that the lightest and heaviest edges of the cyclic
+rank-three block share its middle vertex.  The light edge identifies the
+alternating conjugator, its direction identifies the source order, and `L`
+fixes the repetition count.  That route uses 14 comparisons/arithmetic
+operations.  Without the invariant, the solver must carry out the exact descent
+on large integers; this mechanical-versus-compact gap is the Track-B claim.
+
+## Worked demo
+
+For `make_instance(n=3, repetitions=1, seed=0)`, the complete matrix is
+
+```text
+B =
+  [0,-84,-7,747]
+  [84,0,-10,-9]
+  [7,10,0,11]
+  [-747,9,-11,0]
+L = 8
+```
+
+The answer is `<answer>[2,1,3,0,3,1,3,1]</answer>`, and `verify` returns
+`(True, "ok")`.  Dropping the last entry returns
+`(False, "wrong length: expected 8, received 7")`.  This smallest setting is
+hand-solvable: eight exact mutations can be checked directly, and the invariant
+reduces it to identifying one light edge.
+
+## Difficulty
+
+| Preset | `n` | Alternating repetitions | Answer length | Status |
+|---|---:|---:|---:|---|
+| demo | 3 | 1 | 8 | hand example; skipped by hardener |
+| easy | 10,007 | 4 | 20 | **shipping; bare pool held** |
+| medium | 100,003 | 4 | 20 | larger coefficient height |
+| hard | 1,000,003 | 4 | 20 | larger coefficient height |
+
+`n` grows the exact-integer coefficient height without lengthening the witness.
+`escalate` continues this fixed-length axis before allowing another repetition.
+
+## Gates
+
+| Gate | Result |
+|---|---|
+| G1 | 16/16 planted witnesses verify; all answers JSON-round-trip |
+| G2 | 5/5 corruptions rejected with five distinct reasons |
+| G3 | tagged answer recovered through prose and a Markdown fence |
+| G4 | 0/200,000 reduced-word guesses; exact density `2/4,649,045,868 = 4.302e-10` |
+| G5 | demo enumeration `2/8,748`; shipping density above; strongest failing greedy uses 664 counted operations |
+| G6 | five attacks each 0/8; reference descent 8/8 at 329 operations each |
+| G7 | doubled `n=20,014` builds and verifies with the same 20-atom witness |
+| G8 | 60/60 relabelling/reversal invariance checks; 20/20 unrelated keys distinct |
+| G9 | answer 41 characters, about 11 tokens, 20 atoms; compact route 14 operations; oracle arms recorded below |
+
+## Oracle loop
+
+| Preset | Model | Seed | Solved | Reason |
+|---|---|---:|---|---|
+| easy | Claude Sonnet 5 | 806643057 | no | parsed word failed exact replay |
+| easy | Gemini 3.1 Pro Preview | 1826765562 | no | parsed word failed exact replay |
+| easy | GPT-5.6 Terra | 270591961 | no | parsed word failed exact replay |
+
+All three guessed a repeated numerical sweep rather than the conjugated source
+cycle.  The bare verdict is `hardened` with zero escalations.
+
+## G9 arms
+
+| Arm | Solved / attempts | Verdict |
+|---|---:|---|
+| bare | 0 / 3 | hardened |
+| structural hint | pending | OpenRouter key limit during first run |
+| placebo hint | pending | not yet run |
+
+The structural-versus-placebo conclusion remains pending until both isolated
+`harden.py` runs complete.  This is deliberately not inferred from the bare
+run.  The size/effort portion already passes: 41 characters, 11 estimated
+tokens, 20 atoms, and 14 intended exact operations.
+
+## Use
+
+```python
+from gen_2504_06573 import DIFFICULTY, make_instance, verify
+
+inst = make_instance(seed=7, **DIFFICULTY["easy"])
+ok, reason = verify(inst, inst["answer"])
+assert (ok, reason) == (True, "ok")
+```
+
+From the repository root, emit examples with:
+
+```bash
+scripts/emit.sh 2504.06573 20 easy
+```
+
+## Caveats
+
+This distribution deliberately uses a two-letter alternating conjugator; a
+solver that discovers the light/heavy-edge invariant solves it quickly.  The
+hardness claim is only the no-tool gap, not worst-case hardness and not evidence
+that random quiver-cycle search is hard.  The G4 prior is uniform over all
+reduced words of the required length; it does not model a theorem-aware prior,
+which would put much more mass on conjugated source words.  The attacks do not
+include an external computer-algebra or cluster-algebra package.  Exact replay
+of adversarial wrong words can grow integer bit lengths sharply; keeping the
+shipping word at length 20 is the measured safeguard that replaced an earlier,
+unsafe length-84 ladder.  The G9 hinted/placebo evidence is still externally
+blocked and must be completed before submission.
