Built a verified Track B generator based on Lemma 3.11 and Theorems 4.21, 4.23, and 4.27 of the [paper](https://arxiv.org/html/2504.06573v1).

Deliverables:

- [Generator module](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2504.06573/gen_2504_06573.py)
- [Self-test report](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2504.06573/selftest_report.json)
- [README](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2504.06573/README.md)
- [Bare oracle transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2504.06573/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [Hinted transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2504.06573/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [Placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2504.06573/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

All locally executable gates pass, including:

- G4: 0/200,000 guesses; exact density \(4.302\times10^{-10}\)
- G6: five attacks at 0/8; reference algorithm and compact route both 8/8
- G8: 960/960 symmetry checks
- G9(c): 41 characters, 20 atoms, 32 intended operations

External completion remains blocked: every fresh OpenRouter call returns HTTP 403 “Key limit exceeded.” The preserved earlier bare run held 0/3, but a fresh final-file run and valid hinted/placebo diagnostics require replenishing the OpenRouter key. Error calls were retained and were not counted as model failures.
